# Pievo — environment. Copy to packages/server/.env (or set in your host / Fly secrets).

# --- database (Postgres) ---
# The server runs on Postgres. Two tiers, chosen by whether DATABASE_URL is set:
#
#  1. UNSET (default) → embedded, file-backed pglite at <PIEVO_DATA_DIR>/pgdata.
#     Zero external database — this is the local-dev + light-self-host default,
#     migrates itself in-process at boot. `pnpm dev` just runs; the BUILT server
#     (`pnpm start` / Docker / Fly) additionally requires PIEVO_DB=pglite as an
#     explicit opt-in - without it a missing DATABASE_URL fails the boot loudly
#     (so a lost prod secret can't silently boot an empty ephemeral database).
#  2. SET → postgres-js against your Postgres (e.g. Supabase). Point DATABASE_URL
#     at the TRANSACTION POOLER (:6543) — the driver forces prepare:false for
#     pgBouncer. Set DIRECT_DATABASE_URL to the DIRECT (:5432) session URL; ONLY
#     migrations use it (DDL + advisory lock must not go through the pooler).
#     Both URLs must carry ?sslmode=require for Supabase/any remote Postgres (TLS).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASS@HOST.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require
# DIRECT_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASS@HOST.supabase.com:5432/postgres?sslmode=require
# PIEVO_DB=pglite   # opt the BUILT server into the embedded tier (see tier 1)

# --- data dir ---
# Server-side local artifact bytes; also hosts embedded pglite (tier 1 above).
# A hosted Postgres tier uses it too unless R2 is configured. Persist it as a volume.
# Defaults to ~/.pievo. Must be an ABSOLUTE path — the code does NOT expand `~`, so an
# uncommented `~/.pievo` here would create a literal ./~/.pievo directory.
# PIEVO_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path

# --- artifact blob store (Cloudflare R2, S3-compatible) ---
# Where live-synced loop artifact BYTES are stored (metadata stays in Postgres).
# All four required vars unset ⇒ bytes persist under <PIEVO_DATA_DIR>/blobs.
# Optional explicit selector: local|r2|memory. `memory` is allowed only as an
# explicit ephemeral opt-in and LOSES ALL ARTIFACT BYTES on restart (startup warns).
# It is never a fallback. Without a selector, complete R2 config selects R2;
# otherwise local storage is used.
# PIEVO_BLOB_STORE=local
# Configure R2 for stateless servers. Credentials are never hardcoded.
# PIEVO_R2_ACCOUNT_ID=<cloudflare account id>   # used to derive the endpoint
# PIEVO_R2_BUCKET=<bucket name>
# PIEVO_R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=<r2 access key>
# PIEVO_R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=<r2 secret key>
# Optional. Endpoint defaults to https://<account id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com.
# PIEVO_R2_ENDPOINT=
# Optional. R2 ignores region; "auto" is its convention (the default).
# PIEVO_R2_REGION=auto

# --- artifact storage retention / GC (see gateway/retention.ts) ---
# Exact configured files are collected after each run. Files over 10MB are
# metadata-only; there is no aggregate per-loop storage cap, so monitor the chosen
# byte store. The settings below bound snapshot history and reclaim unreferenced bytes.
# How many of the most recent run snapshots to keep per loop (older ones pruned,
# which unpins their blobs for GC). Default 20.
# PIEVO_SNAPSHOT_RETENTION=20
# Blob GC grace window: a blob whose metadata row is younger than this is never
# collected (concurrency guard). Default 3600000 (1 hour).
# PIEVO_BLOB_GC_GRACE_MS=3600000
# How often the periodic storage-maintenance pass runs (prune snapshots → GC blobs).
# Default 900000 (15 minutes).
# PIEVO_GC_INTERVAL_MS=900000

# --- server ---
# Dev port (vite). Prod (nitro) reads PORT.
PIEVO_PORT=3000
PIEVO_LOG_LEVEL=info
# Stuck-run reclaim: a claimed run that stops heartbeating is provisionally errored
# after this interval (ms), with a bounded late-report reconciliation window.
# PIEVO_RUN_TIMEOUT_MS=1200000
# Circuit breaker: auto-pause a loop after this many consecutive execution errors.
# Default 3; set 0 to disable. Canceled rows are transparent to the streak.
# PIEVO_FAILURE_AUTOPAUSE_STREAK=3
# Machine-route rate limiting (gateway/rateLimit.ts): in-process token buckets on
# every /api/machine/* + /machine/report handler, per-IP (the
# primary flood guard) + per-token (per-machine fairness), 429 past the burst. The
# byte-ingress routes (blob PUT + sync POST) are EXEMPT (already bounded by device
# auth, exact path/hash handshake, and body/file caps). ON by default in a real
# server; OFF under the test runner unless forced. Set PIEVO_RATE_LIMIT=on|off to
# force either way. Defaults below
# comfortably clear a connected daemon's 3s/20s poll — leave unset unless tuning.
# PIEVO_RATE_LIMIT=on
# PIEVO_RL_IP_BURST=240
# PIEVO_RL_IP_PER_SEC=8
# PIEVO_RL_TOKEN_BURST=120
# PIEVO_RL_TOKEN_PER_SEC=4

# --- auth (Better Auth + GitHub). OFF when GITHUB_* are unset → app is open. ---
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Public base URL for YOUR instance's OAuth callback origin, e.g. https://pievo.example.com
# PIEVO_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000
# Session signing secret — set a long random value in prod.
# PIEVO_AUTH_SECRET=
# Comma-separated emails allowed to sign in (empty = anyone allowed).
# PIEVO_ALLOWED_LOGINS=you@example.com,teammate@example.com

# === Daemon (@kky42/pievo, runs on each user's machine) ===
# PIEVO_TOKEN=<device token shown when you add a machine in the UI>
# PIEVO_SERVER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3000   # or your instance's explicit origin
# PIEVO_ROOTS=~/Workspace,~/notes          # cwd jail (empty = unrestricted)
# PIEVO_POLL_MS=3000
# PIEVO_HOME=/absolute/path       # token, server URL, pid/log, and report outbox
# PIEVO_CLAUDE_BIN=claude
# PIEVO_CODEX_BIN=codex
# Coding-agent wall-clock timeout, ms. Unset/0/invalid/negative uses the 12-hour
# default; only a positive value overrides it.
# PIEVO_EXEC_TIMEOUT_MS=900000
